# Exercise: Getting Results from Strands
#
# Strands don't return values directly — they share results
# through channels.
#
# Pattern:
#   1. Create a channel.
#   2. Spawn a strand whose body uses that channel to send its
#      result. The quotation captures the channel by closure
#      when the `[` literal is built (see exercise 01), so no
#      `dup` is needed — the original channel stays on the
#      stack for main to receive on.
#   3. Drop the strand ID.
#   4. Receive the result on main.
#
# Your task: spawn a strand that computes `10 * 5` and sends
# the result through the channel; receive it on main.
#
# Stack walk:
#
#   chan.make                                   ( chan )
#   [ 10 5 i.* swap chan.send drop ]            ( chan [quot] )
#   strand.spawn                                ( chan strand-id )
#   drop                                        ( chan )
#   chan.receive drop                           ( 50 )
#
# When done, delete the marker line below.

# I AM NOT DONE

: compute-in-strand ( -- Int )
    chan.make
    # Your code here:
    # 1. spawn a strand that computes 10 * 5 and sends it
    # 2. drop the strand ID
    # 3. receive from channel and drop the success flag
    drop 0
;

: test-return-value ( -- )
    compute-in-strand
    # Do not edit below this line
    50 test.assert-eq
;
